# 5 SQS long polling - B
Q.append(dict(t="2.1", tp=["Amazon SQS", "Long polling"],
p="A company has 200 worker processes that poll an Amazon SQS standard queue continuously. Most of the day the queue receives only a few messages per minute, yet the company's SQS bill is high because the workers make millions of ReceiveMessage calls that return no messages. Sometimes workers also receive empty responses even when messages are in the queue. The company wants to reduce cost and empty responses without reducing message processing speed. Which solution meets these requirements?",
o=["Increase the visibility timeout of the queue to 12 hours so that workers poll less frequently.",
   "Enable long polling by setting the queue's receive message wait time (ReceiveMessageWaitTimeSeconds) to 20 seconds.",
   "Configure the queue as a delay queue with a delivery delay of 60 seconds so that messages are batched.",
   "Reduce the number of worker processes to 10 and add a sleep of 60 seconds between each ReceiveMessage call."],
c="B",
w=[("Fewer empty receives", "Long polling waits up to 20 seconds for a message to arrive before returning, which greatly reduces the number of empty ReceiveMessage calls (each billed as a request)."),
   ("Fewer false empties", "Long polling queries all SQS servers instead of a subset, eliminating false empty responses."),
   ("No added latency", "A message is returned as soon as one is available.")],
x={"A": "Visibility timeout affects messages that have been received; it does not change how often workers poll.",
   "C": "A delivery delay slows processing and does not reduce empty receives.",
   "D": "Sleeping between polls and reducing workers adds latency and reduces processing capacity during busy periods."},
e=[("High SQS cost from empty receives", "Enable long polling (WaitTimeSeconds up to 20)."),
   ("Short vs long polling", "Short polling samples a subset of servers and returns immediately; long polling waits and checks all servers.")]))
